them by taking some benefit from the confusion (e.g., take the
opportunity to rust-proof some armor)?

Also, how much water do you have, and how many junk potions that
you could dilute instead?  I usually dilute a large stack of object
detection potions (taken from nymphs) in the early middle game, and
(depending on how many I have) maybe also potions of hallucination,
blindness, invisibility, sleeping, paralysis, or anything worth 50
zorkmids that you have a good sized stack of (saving back a couple
of booze for scroll-reading purposes, and maybe a couple of sickness
for dipping your projectiles if you're so inclined).

> [**] I have also two wands of wishing (0:0)

Try to hang onto those until you get scrolls of charging (or, if
scrolls of charging are identified, a magic marker).  As soon as
you have a blessed scroll of charging, charge one of the wands.
One of the wishes will give you a magic marker that will let you
replace the scroll, with marker charges *and* wishes left over.
There's no downside (other than violating wishless conduct).


